From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:14:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, server, explorerframe: Icons of other processes, Aero Snap, ITaskbarList3.

Icons of other processes: a shell draws the icons of other programs'
windows (WM_GETICON, class icons), which in Windows are shared. win32u
now asks the thread that owns such an icon for its pixels
(WM_WINE_GETICONBITS, packed across processes) and draws a copy of its
own, kept in a small cache.

Aero Snap: a window dragged by its caption to the top of a monitor
maximizes when it is let go, to the left or right edge of the screen it
takes that half of the monitor; wineserver keeps where it would go
(set_snap_preview) for dwm.exe to show. A maximized window dragged by
its caption comes out of the maximized state under the pointer.

ITaskbarList3 in explorerframe: progress, overlay icons and the buttons
under the thumbnail (ThumbBar*) go into the table the taskbar reads
(wine/arctic_taskbar.h), icons as pixels; AddTab and DeleteTab reach the
taskbar too.
